This function will execute a series of tests concurrently, up to the specified maximum concurrency limit. It uses `performance.now()` from Node's built-in `perf_hooks` module to measure the duration of each test and logs detailed information about the execution. If any test fails, it will log an error message and continue executing the remaining tests. After each test, it resets a mocking library called `blueslip`.

