["Here's a basic implementation of your requirements in JavaScript:

```javascript
class DataStreamManager {
    constructor(messagingSystem) {
        this.data = [];
        this.isPaused = false;
        this.intervalId = null;
        this.messagingSystem = messagingSystem;
    }

    startCollection(source, interval) {
        if (this.intervalId !== null) return;

        const collectData = () => {
            if (!this.isPaused) {
                // Simulate data collection
                this.data.push({ source: source, timestamp: new Date() });
            } else {
                this.messagingSystem.sendStatusUpdate(source, 'paused');
            }
        };

        collectData();  // Collect initial data immediately
        this.intervalId = setInterval(collectData, interval);
    }

    pauseCollection() {
        if (this.isPaused) return;

        this.isPaused = true;
    }

    resumeCollection() {
        if (!this.isPaused) return;

        this.isPaused = false;
    }

    stopCollection() {
        clearInterval(this.intervalId);
        this.intervalId = null;
    }
}
```
This code creates a `DataStreamManager` class that manages the data collection process from multiple sources. It uses JavaScript's built-in `setInterval` function to periodically collect data, and `clearInterval` to stop the collection. The `startCollection` method starts the collection process for a specific source with a specified interval (in milliseconds). The `pauseCollection` and `resumeCollection` methods pause and resume the data collection respectively.

