            char md5String[MD5_DIGEST_LENGTH * 2 + 1];
            for (int j = 0; j < MD5_DIGEST_LENGTH; ++j) {
                sprintf(&md5String[j * 2], "%02x", fileDatas[i]->md5Digest[j]);
            }

            printf("MD5 hash: %s\n", md5String);
        }

        // Free allocated memory and close the file handle
        free(fileDatas[i]->records);
        fclose(fileDatas[i]->fileHandle);
    }

    return 0;
}
```
This code uses POSIX threads for concurrent processing of files. It reads records from each file, sorts them by key, and calculates the MD5 hash of the file. The main function starts a thread to process each file and waits for all threads to finish before printing the results or logging any errors.
